    3. Build palette 2xN block: outer line = border-key colors, inner line = fill colors. Place on chosen edge.
    4. Generate 2-4 hollow single-color sprites (bbox 3-7 x 3-6) with 1-2 enclosed holes each. For filled sprites, use a palette border-key color and pre-fill holes with the mapped fill color (output state). For the 1 distractor sprite, use a color NOT in palette keys and leave holes as bg.
    5. Place sprites on grid separated from each other and palette by >=1 bg cell.
    6. Save grid as output. To get input, replace all filled-hole cells back to bg.

